    "arctic-epoch": {
      "title": "The Arctic Epoch — Singapore",
      "meta": [
        [
          "Role",
          "Shader Technical Artist"
        ],
        [
          "Team",
          "Group project, 5 people"
        ],
        [
          "Duration",
          "14 weeks"
        ],
        [
          "Tools",
          "Unreal Engine 5, Houdini"
        ]
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Building procedural winter systems for a frozen Singapore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Arctic Epoch is a 14-week group project set in a post-apocalyptic Singapore after a global snowstorm. This case study focuses on my snow and icicle generators, ice shader troubleshooting, and snowflake research."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I developed the piled snow system in Unreal Engine 5 Blueprint and the ice and icicle generator in Houdini. I also resolved rendering issues in a teammate's ice shader. The environment shown here is a collaborative team result."
        },
        {
          "type": "anchor",
          "id": "snow"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Piled Snow Generator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Create snow with visible thickness that conforms to different objects, with controls for coverage and a windswept appearance."
        },
        {
          "type": "embed",
          "src": "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/rGE1g-rqoIk",
          "title": "Snow thickness and texture blend demonstration"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Controlling the snow"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Blueprint tool exposes snow coverage, sparse rate, sphere size, texture, displacement scale and strength, and mesh caching. These controls let me adapt the generated snow to different assets."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Problem — generating snow on large assets"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Large or high-poly models made generation too heavy. Changes to an object's transform or scale also required caching the mesh and generating the snow again."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Solution — generate small, then bake"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I generated snow on objects scaled down to 0.02 to reduce the generation burden, then baked the output as a static mesh for use in the environment."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-d09f8776e1ea8f09.png",
          "alt": "Generated snow meshes applied across environment assets"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Baked snow output across the environment asset set"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Blending snow into the surface"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Alongside the piled geometry, I created a snow texture blend material that could be incorporated into an object's parent material. Blend bias controls the snow amount, while blend sharpness controls the transition."
        },
        {
          "type": "embed",
          "src": "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/3mMGChkBRZ4",
          "title": "Snow texture blend controls"
        },
        {
          "type": "anchor",
          "id": "icicle"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ice & Icicle Generator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I built a generator that grows ice and icicles in response to an input mesh. Controls include seed birth rate, growth speed and length, thickness, shape, and ice coverage."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-c8ae8a0d4d6010ab.gif",
          "alt": "Ice and icicles growing along a Merlion mesh"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Simulated growth conforms to the input mesh"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-716fdf9f4eff47d1.png",
          "alt": "Houdini icicle generator output and controls"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Ice and icicle generation in Houdini"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "From simulation to environment asset"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The tool supports animated growth, but the project used the final simulation frame as its output. The Merlion combines this icicle output with accumulated snow."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-b8969f1b0393b5a4.png",
          "alt": "Merlion in the team environment with snow and icicles applied"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Combined snow and icicle application in the team's environment"
        },
        {
          "type": "anchor",
          "id": "ice-shader"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ice Shader — Rendering & Flickering"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A teammate created the original ice shader. My contribution was to investigate and resolve the transparency and flickering issues that appeared when it was used in the snowstorm environment."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Problem — transparency during the snowstorm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The shader used the scene behind the ice to create a translucent appearance. With the snowstorm's 2D sprites behind it, the ice appeared fully transparent instead of retaining its volume."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-fb5a138a23d807b8.gif",
          "alt": "Before: ice becomes overly transparent against the snowstorm"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Before — transparency breaks down against the snowstorm"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Problem — distant objects flickering"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The ice also showed flickering on distant objects, including the Merlion."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-59115db637a6c66a.gif",
          "alt": "Before: flickering visible on distant ice-covered objects"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Before — unstable appearance on distant ice"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Solution — opaque material with apparent depth"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I switched the shader to opaque and offset its UV coordinates using the camera vector to preserve a volumetric ice appearance. This avoided relying on the scene behind the ice for its translucent look."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-05d26a67734c2bed.gif",
          "alt": "After: opaque ice shader with camera-vector UV offsets"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "After — opaque ice with a volumetric appearance"
        },
        {
          "type": "anchor",
          "id": "snowflake"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Snowflake Generator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Exploratory work — not used in the final playable demo."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I developed a parametric snowflake generator for a planned cinematic introduction, referencing Clifford A. Reiter's A local cellular model for snow crystal growth. Alpha, Beta, and Gamma controls let me explore different growth patterns."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-b27120171dbd41e9.gif",
          "alt": "Cellular snowflake growth simulation in Houdini"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Procedural snowflake growth study"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-299e6f9b0d763c48.png",
          "alt": "Snowflake variations produced by Alpha, Beta, and Gamma parameters"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Exploring parameter-driven snowflake variations"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When the team changed the deliverable from a cinematic to a playable demo, the snowflake introduction was no longer needed. It remains part of the project's research and development."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Team & Contributions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Christine Jung — Shader Technical Artist · Robin Zheng — Technical Artist, Look-Dev Artist · Caiyu Zhang — Environment Artist · Yuxuan Wu — Environment Artist · Laura Yang — Technical Artist, Look-Dev Artist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This case study focuses on my technical art contributions. Environment imagery shows the collaborative project."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Back to the technical breakdown ↑ ↓"
        }
      ],
      "source": "https://christinejung426.com/projects/arctic-epoch/index.html"
    },
    "brick-arch-generator": {
      "title": "Brick Arch Generator",
      "meta": [
        [
          "Role",
          "Solo — tool design and Python scripting"
        ],
        [
          "Tools",
          "Maya, Python, LLM-assisted development"
        ],
        [
          "Used in",
          "European Alleyway"
        ],
        [
          "Year",
          "2026"
        ]
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-c67a0a31c6a540ad.jpg",
          "alt": "Five brick arch variations generated with the Maya tool"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Problem"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Placing bricks one by one along an arch was slow and repetitive, and hand-placed arches all looked the same. I needed many arch shapes with natural silhouette variation for the alleyway's doorways and bridge."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Tool"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/arch-tool-ui.jpg",
          "alt": "Brick Arch Generator control panel in Maya"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The artist-facing panel in Maya: pick an arch curve and a block, set layout and randomness, then rebuild."
        },
        {
          "type": "video",
          "src": "images/web/latest-53d1673886bd5dae.mp4",
          "title": "Project demonstration"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2x speed"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Adjusting block count, scale, taper, and seed rebuilds the arch live in Maya."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Source"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Draw any curve as the arch shape; pick the block mesh to place"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Layout"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Block count, auto-fit block size, mortar gap, wedge taper"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Randomness"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Seed, position and rotation jitter, scale and depth variation, face flips"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Workflow"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Auto rebuild on change, one-click Build / Rebuild, Reset to Defaults"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Works on Existing Geometry"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-876fca2040cd6ef2.gif",
          "alt": "Bricks generated around an arch opening in a wall in Maya"
        },
        {
          "type": "caption",
          "text": "Running the tool along the edge of an arch opening cut into a wall."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The tool is not limited to free-standing arches. Selecting the edge of an existing arch and converting it to a curve gives the tool a path to build along, so the same controls work on openings already modelled into walls."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Applied in Scene"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "images/web/latest-fb93d353d75ea38a.jpg",
          "alt": "Generated brick arches applied to the bridge and doorway in European Alleyway"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How I Built It"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I designed the tool's behavior and controls, and used an LLM to help write the Maya Python. I tested each version in Maya and adjusted it until the output worked in the scene."
        },
        {
          "type": "anchor",
          "id": "related-project"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Related Project"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "European Alleyway"
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "text": "View European Alleyway →",
          "href": "https://christinejung426.com/projects/european-alleyway/index.html"
        }
      ],
      "source": "https://christinejung426.com/projects/Arch_Generator_Tool/index.html"
    },
